tive graph resistance is derived from the field of electric circuit analysis where it is defined as the accumulated effective... more\n\nThis paper studies an interesting graph measure that we call the effective graph resistance. The notion of effective graph resistance is derived from the field of electric circuit analysis where it is defined as the accumulated effective resistance between all pairs of vertices. The objective of the paper is twofold. First, we survey known formulae of the effective graph resistance and derive other representations as well. The derivation of new expressions is based on the analysis of the associated random walk on the graph and applies tools from Markov chain theory. This approach results in a new method to approximate the effective graph resistance.\n\narrow_back_ios\n\narrow_forward_ios\n\ndescriptionView Paperarrow_downwardDownload\n\nAn infinite family of quasi-symmetric designs\n\nby Aart Blokhuis\n\n2015, Journal of Statistical Planning and Inference\n\nPresented is a construction of quasi-symmetric 2-(q 3 , q 2 (q − 1)/2, q(q 3 − q 2\n\ndescriptionView Paperarrow_downwardDownload\n\nLine graph of combinations of generalized Bethe trees: Eigenvalues and energy\n\nby Oscar Rojo\n\n2015\n\nWe characterize the eigenvalues and energy of the line graph L(G) whenever G is (i) a generalized Bethe tree, (ii) a Bethe tree, (iii) a tree defined by generalized Bethe trees attached to a path, (iv) a tree defined by generalized Bethe... more\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCarnets Geol. (https://carnetsgeol.net/cg/DVD-en-index.html)\nciteturn6search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Federica MULÈ, Simone CASATI, Alice PIERI, Marco MERELLA, Andrea DI CENCIO, Giovanni BIANUCCI & Alberto COLLARETA  | HTML  | PDF [832 KB]  | DOI: 10.2110/carnets.2026.2615 ... Triassic (Rhaetian) El Puquén Formation, Chile: Synsedimentary graben, soft-sediment deformation, volcanism, and U-Pb Zircon ag